1. AlphaTims
------------

Project:    AlphaTims
Repository: https://github.com/MannLabs/alphatims
License:    Apache License, Version 2.0
            https://github.com/MannLabs/alphatims/blob/main/LICENSE.txt
Copyright:  Copyright 2020 MannLabs

The full text of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is the same text as the
LICENSE file distributed with OpenTimsTDF.

Ported items (from alphatims/bruker.py, as of release v1.0.10):

  a. parse_decompressed_bruker_binary_type1()
     -> crates/opentimstdf/src/codec.rs, decode_codec1()
     Codec 1 per-scan signed-int32 TOF-delta / intensity walk.

  b. process_frame(), compression_type == 1 branch
     -> crates/opentimstdf/src/reader.rs, Reader::decode_peaks_codec1()
     Codec 1 frame header (bin_size, scan_count), scan offset table and
     its rebasing by 8 + 4 * (scan_count + 1).

  c. TimsTOF._import_data_from_d_folder(), metadata-based m/z estimate
     -> crates/opentimstdf/src/reader.rs, Reader::calibration()
     Linear-in-sqrt(m/z) model between MzAcqRangeLower and
     MzAcqRangeUpper over DigitizerNumSamples, with the 5 m/z widening
     for "Bruker otofControl". OpenTimsTDF follows the OpenTIMS
     implementation of this model (item 2b below).

Changes made by OpenTimsTDF: translated from Python/Numba to Rust;
emitted TOF indices are 0-based (tof - 1); all reads are bounds-checked
and malformed input returns an error instead of panicking; LZF
decompression is done by OpenTimsTDF's own decoder instead of the
python-lzf package.


2. OpenTIMS
-----------

Project:    OpenTIMS (opentims++)
Repository: https://github.com/michalsta/opentims
License:    MIT License
            https://github.com/michalsta/opentims/blob/master/LICENCE

Ported items (from src/opentims++/):

  a. tof2mz_converter.cpp, OpenSourceTof2MzConverter and
     scan2inv_ion_mobility_converter.cpp, OpenSourceScan2ImConverter
     -> crates/opentimstdf/src/calibration.rs, Calibration
     tof_to_mz / mz_to_tof and scan_to_inv_mobility /
     inv_mobility_to_scan, including the round-half-up, clamp-at-zero
     inverse.

  b. tof2mz_converter.cpp, OpenSourceTof2MzConverterFactory::produce()
     and scan2inv_ion_mobility_converter.cpp,
     OpenSourceScan2ImConverterFactory::produce()
     -> crates/opentimstdf/src/reader.rs, Reader::calibration()
     GlobalMetadata keys used, the otofControl widening, scan_max taken
     as MAX(Frames.NumScans), and the validity checks.

  c. opentims.cpp, TimsFrame::decode()
     -> crates/opentimstdf/src/codec.rs, decode_codec2()
     Codec 2 scan header (peak count = header[scan + 1] / 2), TOF
     accumulator starting at UINT32_MAX, and the last scan taking the
     remaining peaks.

Changes made by OpenTimsTDF: translated from C++ to Rust; the decoder
is total (bounds-checked, never panics on malformed input); metadata is
read through rusqlite; errors are returned as Rust values.

